  "notes": [
    "## Event to field reasoning - Reservation By Code\n\n- **Reservation Placed** -> sets `Id`, `Code`, `Email`, `Start`, `End`, `NumberOfPeople` - the only source event. This is a single-record lookup keyed on `Code`, not a list.\n\n### Why `Id` is projected even though the screen never displays it\n\nThe `Find Your Reservation` screen carries a field `Id` mapped to `Cancel Reservation.Id`. The guest types a code, never an id - so that value has to come from somewhere on the page. It comes from here. Without `Id` on this read model, the cancel command would have an input with no traceable source.\n\nThis is the reason the cancel-by-code flow was modelled as a lookup slice rather than a bare `Cancel Reservation(code)` command: resolving code -> id happens in a read model *before* the command is issued, so the command still validates against its own event stream and never against a projection.\n\n### Fan-in\n\nOne source event. No split needed."
